---
/**
 * After the command: what the installer does (deploy/install.sh and installer/lib), how to
 * check the install is healthy (the bemmoly command, /healthz, Settings › System status), the
 * setup wizard (apps/web use-setup-wizard), turning modules on, and AI, which is optional and
 * off until an admin turns it on (the 0.5.0 release notes).
 */
import { WHAT_YOU_GET } from '../../data/self-hosting.ts';
import CodeBlock from '../site/CodeBlock.astro';
import Icon from '../site/Icon.astro';
import Section from '../site/Section.astro';

const HEALTH = `$ sudo bemmoly status
$ sudo bemmoly doctor
$ curl -fsS https://work.example.com/healthz`;
---

<Section title="What happens" id="what-it-does">
  <ul>
    <li>Checks the machine: the system, memory, disk, ports 80 and 443, and DNS.</li>
    <li>Installs Docker Engine and the Compose plugin if they are missing, or uses yours.</li>
    <li>
      Writes <code>/var/bemmoly</code>: the Compose file, the Caddyfile, a <code>.env</code> with
      freshly generated secrets, and the <code>data</code> and <code>backups</code> folders.
    </li>
    <li>
      Starts Postgres 18 and the app, which applies its schema changes as it starts, then asks for a
      certificate for your domain.
    </li>
    <li>
      Schedules the nightly backup, installs the <code>bemmoly</code> command and prints your
      address.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If the domain does not point at the machine yet, it starts with a self-signed certificate, and a
    real one follows by itself once DNS does. Keep a copy of <code>/var/bemmoly/.env</code>
    somewhere safe: it holds the key that decrypts stored credentials and the backup passphrase, and
    backups do not contain it.
  </p>
  <ul class="grid list-none! gap-3 pl-0! sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
    {WHAT_YOU_GET.map((item) => (
      <li class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 rounded-window border border-line bg-side p-4 pl-4! dark:bg-card">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2 text-14 font-semibold text-tx">
          <Icon name="check-circle" class="text-green-tx" />
          {item.title}
        </span>
        <span class="text-13 leading-brief text-tx-2">{item.body}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</Section>

<Section title="Check it is healthy" id="health">
  <CodeBlock code={HEALTH} label="On the server; use your own domain" copy />
  <p>
    <code>bemmoly status</code> shows the containers, the version, the database size, the queue, the
    last backup and the certificate. <code>bemmoly doctor</code> runs the installer’s checks and the
    app’s health checks again and says how to fix what fails. <code>/healthz</code> answers when the
    app is up. In the app, Settings › System status shows the same checks.
  </p>
</Section>

<Section title="First login" id="first-login">
  <p>
    The first visit runs the setup wizard: name the workspace, create your admin account on your
    server, bring your data or start clean, invite your team, choose what AI may do or skip it, and
    pick the workspace’s look. Everything can be changed later in Settings. Invitations go out
    through your mail server, set in Settings › Email delivery.
  </p>
</Section>

<Section title="Turn on Work and Docs" id="modules">
  <p>
    <strong>Modules start switched off.</strong> To track issues or write pages, open Settings ›
    Manage modules, turn on Work, Docs or both, and choose who can use each: nobody yet, everyone,
    or specific teams. Until then, people see the shell without them.
  </p>
</Section>

<Section title="Set up AI (optional)" id="ai">
  <p>
    Bemmoly works fully without AI, and AI stays off until an admin turns it on. To use it, open
    Settings › AI and models, add a provider from the models.dev catalog with its key, or a model on
    your own network by its address, and press Test connection. Pick a model for each role, then
    turn AI on for the workspace.
  </p>
  <p>
    Then summaries with their sources, answers from your docs, help in the editor and plans you
    confirm appear, all drawn in lilac. Settings decides whether page and issue content is sent,
    which spaces and projects are excluded, whether AI may change data, and a monthly budget. Turned
    off again, every AI surface disappears and nothing more is sent.
  </p>
</Section>
